## 1. MAIN OBJECTIVE

Upgrade the existing My Money Manager application into three separate, independently accessible application experiences:

1. User Application
2. Admin Application
3. Staff Application

All three applications must have:
- Separate URLs.
- Separate login experiences.
- Separate app branding and logos.
- Separate PWA installation experiences.
- Separate app manifests and service-worker scopes.
- Role-based permissions.
- Appropriate notifications.
- Responsive mobile and desktop layouts.

Additionally, create a complete Website & App Management Control Center inside the Admin Panel.

The Admin must be able to manage the website, application branding, logos, colors, app names, notifications, website content, and other configurable settings from one place.

All configuration changes must synchronize across connected applications in real time without requiring users to manually refresh their pages.

**IMPORTANT:** First inspect the existing codebase, framework, routing, authentication, database, hosting, PWA implementation, service workers, and notification architecture. Adapt the existing project rather than rebuilding it unnecessarily.

Preserve existing users, financial records, transactions, Udhaar data, UPI QR functionality, and all existing modules.

