# 7. SEPARATE PWA INSTALLATION FOR ALL THREE APPS

All three applications must have independent installation experiences.

### User App

- Own PWA manifest.
- Own app name.
- Own short name.
- Own icons.
- Own theme color.
- Own background color.
- Own start URL.
- Own installation prompt.

### Admin App

- Separate manifest.
- Admin App name.
- Admin App logo.
- Admin-specific icons.
- Admin-specific theme color.
- Admin start URL: `/myadmin`.
- Admin-specific installation experience.

### Staff App

- Separate manifest.
- Staff App name.
- Staff App logo.
- Staff-specific icons.
- Staff-specific theme color.
- Staff start URL: `/mystaff`.
- Staff-specific installation experience.

### PWA isolation

Use separate service-worker scopes wherever the architecture supports it.

Ensure:
- User App installation opens the User App.
- Admin App installation opens `/myadmin`.
- Staff App installation opens `/mystaff`.
- Each installed app displays the correct branding.
- Each application has appropriate navigation and login behavior.
- Updates to one app do not accidentally break another app's cache or installation.

Do not simply use one generic manifest for all three apps.

### Install buttons

Provide an Install App option in:
- User App settings or existing install prompt.
- Admin App settings.
- Staff App settings.

Display the installation prompt only when supported by the browser.

If the app is already installed:
- Do not repeatedly show the install prompt.
- Show an Installed state or appropriate guidance.

If installation is unavailable:
- Display clear browser-specific installation instructions.

### App icons and installed app updates

When Admin replaces an app logo:

1. Save the new image.
2. Update the relevant manifest icon configuration.
3. Use versioned icon URLs or safe cache-busting.
4. Update the relevant service-worker cache.
5. Notify active clients that branding has changed.
6. Make updated icons available to supported browser/OS installation environments.

Important technical limitation:

Some browsers and operating systems cache installed PWA icons independently. A website cannot guarantee that every already-installed home-screen icon changes instantly on every device.

Implement the best supported update mechanism and provide clear instructions when a browser or operating system requires reinstalling or refreshing the installed shortcut.

Do not claim guaranteed immediate OS-level icon replacement.

